# Day 1: Setup (workbook rows 5 and 6, TL steps 1 and 2)
# How to run: install the VS Code extension "REST Client" (by Huachao Mao),
# then click the small "Send Request" link that appears above each request.
# Before EVERY request: write your guessed status code in notes/day01.md, then send.

@baseUrl = https://api.hubapi.com
@token = {{$dotenv HUBSPOT_TOKEN}}

### Row 6: Check the token works
# 200 = token works, 401 = token wrong, 403 = token valid but missing scope
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Extra: account details (portalId = your Hub ID; accountType should be a test account)
GET {{baseUrl}}/account-info/v3/details
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Experiment: send a wrong token on purpose and read the error
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/contacts?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer wrong-token-123

### Scope check: crm.objects.companies.read (403 = scope missing)
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/objects/companies?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Scope check: crm.schemas.contacts.read (needed on Day 3 for custom properties)
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/properties/contacts/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Scope check: crm.schemas.companies.read
GET {{baseUrl}}/crm/v3/properties/companies/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
